# 145. Binary Tree Postorder Traversal

## APPROACH: BINARY TREE POSTORDER TRAVERSAL

Idea:
Postorder Traversal follow karta hai: Left -> Right -> Root (L-R-N).
Pehle poora left subtree process hoga, fir poora right subtree, aur last me current node ki value add hogi.

--------------------------------------------------

APPROACH (Recursive / DFS)

1. Ek result list (`ans`) initialize karo.

2. Ek recursive helper function call karo: `helper(ans, root)`.

3. Base Case:
   Agar `root == null` hai, simply `return` kar jao (subtree end).

4. Left child ke liye recursive call karo:
   `helper(ans, root.left)`

5. Right child ke liye recursive call karo:
   `helper(ans, root.right)`

6. Dono subtrees complete hone ke baad current node ki value list me add karo:
   `ans.add(root.val)`

7. Final list `ans` return kar do.

--------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE

Tree:
    1
     \
      2
     /
    3

Calls:
- Call 1 -> Left of 1 is null
- Call Right of 1 (node 2)
  - Call Left of 2 (node 3)
    - Left & Right of 3 are null -> ans.add(3)
  - Call Right of 2 is null
  - Node 2 dono side se free -> ans.add(2)
- Node 1 dono side se free -> ans.add(1)

Result: [3, 2, 1]

--------------------------------------------------

WHY RECURSION?

- Postorder bottom-up process follow karta hai (pehle leaves, fir parents).
- Recursive call stack bottom-most leaves par pehle execute hoke unwinding ke time parents ko process karta hai, jo natural L-R-N sequence deta hai.

--------------------------------------------------

COMPLEXITY

N = Total number of nodes in tree
H = Height of binary tree

Time:
O(N) -> Har node exactly ek baar visit hoti hai.

Space:
O(H) -> Recursive call stack height par depend karta hai.
Worst case (skewed tree): O(N)
Best/Average case (balanced tree): O(log N)
*(Excluding output list)*

--------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW POINT

Postorder means "Node Last Me" (Left -> Right -> Root).
Use cases: Deleting a tree, bottom-up calculations (like calculating tree height, diameter, or evaluating expression trees).
Follow-up me interviewer iterative solution maangta hai:
1. 2 Stacks approach: Modified Preorder (Root -> Right -> Left) ko Stack 1 se Stack 2 me dalo, stack 2 pop karne par (Left -> Right -> Root) deta hai.
2. 1 Stack approach: Extra `prev` pointer maintain karke track karte hain ki right child visit ho chuka hai ya nahi.

--------------------------------------------------

# CODE:

import java.util.*;

/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * public class TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode left;
 *     TreeNode right;
 *     TreeNode() {}
 *     TreeNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     TreeNode(int val, TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
 *         this.val = val;
 *         this.left = left;
 *         this.right = right;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> postorderTraversal(TreeNode root) {
        List<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();
        helper(ans, root);
        return ans;        
    }

    private void helper(List<Integer> ans, TreeNode root) {
        // Base case
        if (root == null) {
            return;
        }

        // Process Left -> Right -> Root
        helper(ans, root.left);
        helper(ans, root.right);
        ans.add(root.val);
    }
}
